hwmon: lm75: Maemo critical-temperature attributes for the N8x0 TMP105

Maemo's DSME (libtemperature, loaded by the initfs DSME) finds the hwmon
device whose device/name is "tmp105", writes device/temp1_crit (80000)
and device/temp1_crit_hyst (75000), then waits on
device/temp1_crit_alarm with select() and powers the device off when it
reads '1'. Those were attributes of Nokia's 2.6.21 tmp105 driver; lm75
has temp1_max/temp1_max_hyst on the hwmon device, so the thermal
shutdown never armed.

With CONFIG_SENSORS_LM75_N8X0_CRIT, on the N800/N810 the TMP105's I2C
device gets the three attributes: temp1_crit and temp1_crit_hyst are
the limit registers (T_HIGH, T_LOW), and the alarm follows the TMP105
comparator (set at temp1_crit, cleared below temp1_crit_hyst), polled
every 2 s. DSME select()s the alarm for reading; 2.6.21's sysfs_poll()
reported nothing until a change, kernfs reports attributes readable at
all times and DSME spun (~240 wakeups/s in QEMU). So the alarm is a
kernfs file whose poll, as then, reports only a change.

